# Sanctioned importers of pkg/std/os/sys from OUTSIDE the os family (pkg/std/os*).
# One <repo-relative-file> per line; comments start with #.  See
# os-sys-consumers.sh for the rule (os/sys is the os abstraction's private
# libc-syscall foundation; OS-specific code must not leak outside of os).
#
# Use sparingly — a real importer outside pkg/std/os* almost always means the
# code should reach OS services through pkg/std/os / pkg/std/os/process instead.
#
# The VM's stdlib-injection glue imports every native stdlib package — including
# os/sys — to register it as a native instance so its __c_calls run natively
# under the bytecode interpreter (see stdPkgs() / design-syscall.md).  This
# INJECTS os/sys as infrastructure; it does not consume it as OS-specific code.
pkg/binate/interp/externs.bn
